Matrices in this directory come from the SuiteSparse Matrix Collection
(https://sparse.tamu.edu), group HB: the Harwell-Boeing Collection assembled
by Iain Duff, Roger Grimes and John Lewis at the Rutherford Appleton
Laboratory and Boeing Computer Services.

The SuiteSparse Matrix Collection licenses the matrices under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0), reproduced in
LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0.txt (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). It asks
that the collection be cited:

  T. A. Davis and Y. Hu, "The University of Florida Sparse Matrix
  Collection", ACM Transactions on Mathematical Software, 38(1), 2011.

The .mtx files in corpus/ are the unmodified Matrix Market files as
downloaded from https://suitesparse-collection-website.herokuapp.com/MM/HB/<name>.tar.gz
on 2026-09-21, with the original banner and comment blocks intact.

Test and benchmark inputs either copy these files unchanged or adapt them
(a principal submatrix, the symmetric part, an added diagonal, and similar);
an adapted matrix carries a comment line naming the source matrix and
stating the change.
